<title>SPAIN: Beet sugar content at 17.24 pct in southern Spain.</title>
<headline>Beet sugar content at 17.24 pct in southern Spain.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average sugar content of beet in southern Spain tested at 17.24 percent at the factory gate on July 20, slightly higher than last year but within a normal range, the National Sugar Beet association told Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A test on July 13 showed sugar content at 17.33 percent.</p>
<p>The southern crop, which represents about a third of Spain's total beet harvest, draws to a close early next month.</p>
<p>Field tests on the northern harvest are available as of mid-September, a spokesman for the association said.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
